<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wheat sowing had finished throughout Argentina by September 20, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Most wheat in Buenos Aires province is between germination and tillering, while wheat in Santa Fe, Cordoba and Entre Rios is between tillering and jointing. La Pampa wheat is mainly tillering. Generally, wheat in southern and central Buenos Aires and La Pampa was in good condition. But northwestern Buenos Aires needed good rains fast to avoid losses in yields. Wheat in Cordoba, Santa Fe and Entre Rios was in critical need of rain. Recent rain helped speed maize sowing.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
